title: The Strike Committee Says No
subtitle: A district strike committee defies the Zentrale.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year >= 1919 and year <= 1920 and time >= 6 and crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and ending_id = 0 and strike_count >= 1 and e20_committee_line = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 1
on-arrival: {!
var d = RG.target('strike');
Q.e20_committee_d = d;
Q.e20_committee_name = Q.sys_target_name;
Q.e20_committee_trade = Q.sys_target_trade;
Q.e20_committee_ours = Q.sys_target_ours;
Q.e20_committee_faction = Q.sys_target_faction_name;
Q.e20_committee_nb = Q.sys_target_neighbour_name ? 1 : 0;
Q.e20_committee_nb_name = Q.sys_target_neighbour_name || 0;
Q.e20_committee_rep = Q.sys_target_repression;
!}

= The Strike Committee Says No

In [+ e20_committee_name +], [+ e20_committee_trade +] have been out for weeks. Our comrades sit on the strike committee, [? if e20_committee_ours = 1 : most of them loyal to the Zentrale. ?][? if e20_committee_ours = 0 : most of them followers of the [+ e20_committee_faction +]. ?] The Zentrale has told them the strike cannot win alone and must be ended in good order.

The committee has voted the Zentrale's letter down and printed the vote. [? if e20_committee_rep >= 55 : The Security Police are in the town in force. ?]

- @spread: Call out [+ e20_committee_nb_name +] in solidarity.
- @order: Order our comrades off the committee.
- @envoy: Send a member of the Zentrale to settle the strike.

@spread
subtitle: [? if lock_councils = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] A bigger strike, or a bigger defeat.
view-if: e20_committee_nb = 1
choose-if: lock_councils < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_councils == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e20_committee_line = 2;
RG.spreadStrike(Q.e20_committee_d);
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: 6, repression: 6});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

By the end of the week the works in [+ e20_committee_nb_name +] are out too, and the police have twice as many pickets to break.

@order
subtitle: The strike ends. The district will remember who left it.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_committee_line = 3;
RG.endStrike(Q.e20_committee_d);
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: -14, members: -0.04});
Q.unity += 2;
!}

Our comrades resign from the committee, and the strike crumbles within days. Some of the men who went back tear up their party cards.

@envoy
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. A settlement, perhaps a decent one.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds to send anyone.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_committee_line = 4;
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e20_committee_ok = Math.random() < 0.55 ? 1 : 0;
RG.endStrike(Q.e20_committee_d, Q.e20_committee_ok ? 'won' : undefined);
RG.district(Q.e20_committee_d, {loyalty: 3});
Q.lean_unionist += 1;
!}

[? if e20_committee_ok = 1 : The Zentrale's man comes out of three days with the employers holding a wage rise and a promise of no victimisations. The committee grumbles, and takes it. ?][? if e20_committee_ok = 0 : The Zentrale's man comes back with a promise of arbitration. The strike ends without a victory, and without a rout. ?]
